 history command (sase-a1.1)"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"a64f6d64fef5540a986c99287df8bf29f5be62074a02003689107b7e4c07b57d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/chat.md","size_bytes":10531},"commits":{"digest":"ce69c9bd38fe4247374d326a264c5fe10bced3dbc4c8c37d91c6757e65b5debb","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/commits.json","size_bytes":222},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"70a200cb0d2299e877311111dec9583cdee49b85bc1959349fcaa4d4c8a4eb82","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/meta.json","size_bytes":5392},"prompt":{"digest":"901801baedda38e27fcfe0552513f8db588552ef333a12e60c3dd633790ca37d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":182},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"932dde606f824efdf82245a2e3a9630bd891f79d69c076c780d8865c55719d0b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":15533},"state":{"digest":"f87f931a4085837ad79da729f88c1f771784706df93b55363d89ad04fee1bbf4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1/state.json","size_bytes":183}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1","local_name":"sase-a1.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-a1","agent_clan_generation":"20260727123537","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-a1.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-a1[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Expose bead history and make bead completion truthful[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A closed bead is trustworthy evidence and a bead's working history [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]is readable: every note revision the event streams already hold is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]reachable from the CLI, notes accumulate instead of being [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]overwritten, the ~509 beads whose notes lost earlier revisions can [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]be repaired, closing a parent no longer silently manufactures [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]completion for descendants nobody worked, every closure records a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]done/canceled/superseded resolution, and reopening a bead reopens [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the ancestors whose completion claim it invalidates.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bead_history_truthful_close.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Read the event streams as a per-bead timeline[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]history[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]history: add a Rust replay API that turns a bead's event stream into an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ordered list of field-level changes, expose it through the PyO3 binding,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and ship `sase bead history` as its first reader.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Record and display how a bead was resolved[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]resolution[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolution: add a stored done/canceled/superseded resolution to the bead[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record end to end — wire, close event, SQLite mirror, Python model, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the close CLI — and surface it with the close reason, which no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]human-readable surface prints today.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Append to bead notes instead of replacing them[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]note[dim] · [dim][/dim]after history[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]note: add an atomic append-a-note mutation in the Rust core and a `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead note` verb, so recording progress no longer destroys what an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]earlier writer left behind.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop closing descendants nobody worked[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]invariant[dim] · [dim][/dim]after resolution[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]invariant: make the parent-close cascade explicit rather than silent — [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reject a close whose descendants were never closed on their own, require[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]force plus a reason and a non-done resolution to override, record which [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]descendants were swept, and reopen closed ancestors whenever a bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]leaves the closed state.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Find and repair notes lost to overwrite[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]recover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after history, note[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]recover: detect beads whose current notes dropped text an earlier [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]revision held, report them, and offer a confirmation-gated repair that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-appends the dropped revisions with provenance.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Land the new surfaces as one coherent contract[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]integrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after invariant, recover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]integrate: reconcile the two halves into one documented contract — bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs, the generated `sase_beads` skill, the land and phase xprompts, the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]published core version window — and produce end-to-end acceptance [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]evidence against the live store.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-a1","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-a1.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-d0b158452d3993aa49415939ed708b67","started_at":"2026-07-27T16:35:49.380076+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.6","bbugyi200.athena.sase-a1.land"]}
